cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  This code accompanies the manuscript "Condensates increase the
  frequency of transcription" (Eppert, Halingstad, et al.).
type: software
title: >-
  2026_eppert_halingstad_3state_transcription: Code and data for
  condensate-driven transcriptional bursting
authors:
  - family-names: "Halingstad"
    given-names: "Ethan V."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0612-385X"
  - family-names: "Shrinivas"
    given-names: "Krishna"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4167-9385"
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/shrinivaslab/2026_eppert_halingstad_3state_transcription
abstract: >-
  Code and data to accompany the manuscript "Condensates increase the
  frequency of transcription," which examines cofactor (CoF)
  condensate-driven transcriptional bursting. Simulates a stochastic
  three-state promoter model, comparing a soluble cofactor regime
  against a condensate-forming cofactor regime.
keywords:
  - biomolecular condensates
  - transcriptional bursting
  - stochastic gene expression
  - Gillespie simulation
  - phase separation
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
